macOS: Decide on the Liquid Glass opt out by the SDK of the application

Not upstream: qt_apple_runningWithLiquidGlass() in the 6.10, 6.11 and
6.12 branches and in dev (checked in October 2026) still reads the key
by the version of the running system.

qt_apple_runningWithLiquidGlass() reads UIDesignRequiresCompatibility
from the Info.plist only when running on macOS older than 27. Its
comment says it was unclear whether building against the Xcode 27 SDK
or running on macOS 27 disables the opt out, and goes with the latter.
It is the SDK. Apple's documentation for the key says the system
ignores it when you build for macOS 27 or later, and an AppKit
application measured on macOS 27 has NSButton, NSPopUpButton,
NSTextField and NSSegmentedControl 20/20/21/22 pt tall when built
against the macOS 26.2 SDK with the key set, and 24 pt when built
against the 27 SDK, with the key or without it.

So an application built with Xcode 26 and the key set gets the old
AppKit controls on macOS 27, while QMacStyle lays them out with the
Liquid Glass metrics. By the same documentation an application built
with Xcode 27 and the key set gets it the other way round on macOS 26.
Check the SDK the application was built against instead of the
running system. Applications without the key are not affected.

--- a/qtbase/src/corelib/kernel/qcore_mac.mm
+++ b/qtbase/src/corelib/kernel/qcore_mac.mm
@@ -346,11 +346,11 @@
         if (QMacVersion::currentRuntime().majorVersion() < 26)
             return false;
 
-        // Word on the street is that the opt out will only work for
-        // macOS 26, but it's not clear whether building against the
-        // Xcode 27 SDK is what will disable it, or simply running on
-        // macOS 27. Let's go with the latter for now.
-        if (QMacVersion::currentRuntime().majorVersion() < 27) {
+        // AppKit honors the opt out as long as the application is built
+        // against an SDK older than 27, on macOS 27 as well, and ignores
+        // it in applications built against the macOS 27 SDK on any macOS
+        // version. So it is the SDK that decides, not the running system.
+        if (QMacVersion::buildSDK(QMacVersion::ApplicationBinary).majorVersion() < 27) {
             const id liquidGlassOptOut = [NSBundle.mainBundle
                 objectForInfoDictionaryKey:@"UIDesignRequiresCompatibility"];
             if (liquidGlassOptOut && [liquidGlassOptOut boolValue])
